{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "step": "3",
  "purpose": "Publishable-content policy read by ehr_evidence_app.quality.publication. It declares publishable types, forbidden path categories, required .gitignore probes, high-confidence secret signatures, the machine-specific user-path rule, the numeric patient-identifier rule and the explicit placeholder rules. The script holds the same rules as fixed minimums: this file may tighten them but cannot weaken them.",
  "notes": [
    "Only this repository's config directory may supply the policy. It cannot choose the repository, the Git binary or any audit scope.",
    "Patterns are regular expressions, not examples. \\x22, \\x27 and \\x60 stand for the double quote, single quote and backtick.",
    "A named group 'secret' marks the value checked against the placeholder rules; otherwise the whole match is checked. Private-key and token-shape signatures are never exempt.",
    "Placeholder markers count only as whole tokens with no letter or digit on either side; placeholder patterns must match the whole value.",
    "The unquoted_assignment category is not applied to Python sources, where an unquoted value is an expression; quoted Python literals are covered by secret_assignment.",
    "Synthetic-fixture exemption applies to the patient-identifier rule only: a file beneath a fixture root whose name has synthetic as a whole token, or a test module whose opening docstring line declares it synthetic."
  ],
  "max_candidate_bytes": 1048576,
